    narr:generatedFrom "37b6bf2c84965cc245e031aab2e50ce7a0484a10" ;
    narr:narration """Tanya's voice here is a chair converting deliberation into settled rules across two dated meetings. In the first she [bounds the meeting against a steering-group deadline](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_1), [states her landing position before hearing others](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8), and [prices the two cutovers as contained versus unbounded risk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13); she probes rather than accepts ([asking where a two-week figure comes from](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_18)), then [ratifies the reasoning on the record](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_20) and [orders the reporting constraint written as a rule, not guidance](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_31), adding a [political framing that keeps reference-data blame on the vendor](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_39) before [rehearsing her steering-group script](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_42). A week later she [briefs a newcomer on the settled shape](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_2), [restates the one-at-a-time rule](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_7), and — the notable move — [adopts someone else's sharper version of her own argument](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_13), [committing to lead with it](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_17). The register stays casual-but-commanding, antithesis and parallelism dominant in her org lane, with consultation and legitimate authority run side by side.""" ;
